          "label": "<p>A 58-year-old man with atrial fibrillation and a mechanical mitral valve prosthe</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 58-year-old man with atrial fibrillation and a mechanical mitral valve prosthesis requires long-term anticoagulation. Which agent is the most appropriate choice?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Apixaban</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>DOACs like apixaban are first-line for non-valvular atrial fibrillation, but they perform worse in patients with mechanical heart valves and are contraindicated in this setting.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Warfarin</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Mechanical heart valves require warfarin — it is the only anticoagulant with proven safety and efficacy in this setting. DOACs have shown worse outcomes here.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Enoxaparin</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>LMWH is used for short-term bridging (e.g., perioperatively) but is not suitable for long-term outpatient anticoagulation in mechanical valve patients.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Dabigatran</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Dabigatran was specifically tested in mechanical valve patients and caused more thromboembolic and bleeding events than warfarin. It is contraindicated in this setting.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Remember the rule: mechanical heart valves require warfarin only. DOACs perform worse in this specific population and are contraindicated despite being first-line in non-valvular atrial fibrillation."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. This illustrates the key principle from this section: newer isn't always better. Mechanical heart valves remain a firm indication for warfarin over DOACs."
                }
              ],
